## Context

Addition 3 of `design/2026-11-12-guichet-inter-repo-dialogue.md` § 5: a return path for blocked askers. In the trial,
consequences of fixes reached adopters only through tracker log lines
(K-G1, K-G2).

## Scope

- A blocked asker parks its own ticket: `Blocked-by: <receiver>/<NNNN>`
  (erg accepts another repository's ticket as a URI reference; git-erg
  `design/erg-manual.md`, rule 9), the `deferred` label (an unresolved
  reference is optimistic for readiness, so the label gates it), and a log
  line. It does not wait.
- The asker's `/molt` reads each such reference in the receiver's store;
  when the receiver's ticket is closed it removes `deferred` and the
  `Blocked-by:` line and logs `unblocked by <receiver> <NNNN>, closed in
  <commit>`. Nothing is written into the receiver.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Parking and release described in `rules/workflow.md` § Cross-project
      work and implemented in `/molt`.
- [ ] Between two of the author's repositories, a parked ticket returns to
      the ready queue once the receiver's ticket closes; a sibling-path and
      an absolute-URI reference both work.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
